          "title": "Toppling the Hierarchy in Byte-level Language Modeling",
          "title_zh": "推翻字节级语言建模中的层级结构",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.00463v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.00463",
          "summary": "Examines why byte-level models fail to perfectly manipulate characters, finding that the hierarchical byte-to-word-to-byte design itself limits character-level understanding, with pure byte-level models consistently outperforming hierarchical variants on character manipulation tasks. Layer ablations further indicate byte-level attention as the primary mechanism, framing a trade-off between computational efficiency and fine-grained character understanding.",
