          "title_zh": "探索语言智能体与非语言智能体的协作",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.00474v2",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.00474",
          "summary": "Introduces LLAMIA-Bench, six collaborative chess tasks spanning behavioral imitation, state assessment and natural-language explanation, to test whether verbalizing a non-language agent's continuous representations into text creates a bottleneck. It proposes latent state internalization, which projects those representations into the LLM token stream as learned state tokens; a 14B model trained this way matches or exceeds task specialists and frontier models including GPT-5.1 with tool access, and generalizes out of distribution.",
