          "title_zh": "一种用于学习路径规划的量子-经典混合神经网络",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.00489v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.00489",
          "summary": "Asks whether small quantum neural networks can replace parameter-heavy modules inside a competitive attention-based routing model for the capacitated vehicle routing problem. Encoder feed-forward replacement reduces model parameters by 56.6% while staying close to the classical neural baseline at small and medium instance sizes, though the gap grows for larger instances; the authors report no quantum advantage or solver dominance.",
