          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.00460",
          "summary": "Introduces Animus, a synthetic financial dataset in which predicting customer income requires aggregating up to tens of thousands of transactions, exposing the constrained neighborhood budgets of relational foundation models. Three recent models achieve R^2 of at most 0.18 on the raw representation, while a single routine temporal pre-aggregation step recovers R^2 up to 0.65, questioning readiness for high-cardinality real-world data.",
